course: dictionary
lesson: 2046
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. Conker can mean a shiny seed, or a game. To find the right meaning, read the words around it, which is the context. «Collect conkers, acorns and pine cones for crafts» is about seeds you pick up from the ground.
explain: Look for clue words. Collect, crafts and pine cones point to nature. «The game of conkers has a world championship» points to play, because a championship is a contest. Ask yourself: does my meaning fit? If you swap in "seed" here, the sentence makes no sense, so the game meaning is right.
explain: Check every sentence for clues. In «Maddie came down with conkers in every pocket», the pockets are full of seeds she has collected. Two meanings, one word: the context decides which one the writer means.
fact: A conker is the shiny brown seed of a horse chestnut tree.
fact: The seed grows inside a spiky green case.
fact: Conkers is also a children's game, played mainly in the UK and Ireland.
fact: In the game, you put a conker on a string and try to break the other player's conker.
fact: Conkers are poisonous to eat, unlike sweet chestnuts, so never eat them.
exercise: «Collect conkers, acorns and pine cones for crafts.» In this sentence, what is a conker? | A kind of sweet | A game played with a ball | A type of shoe | *A shiny brown seed from a horse chestnut tree
exercise: «The game of conkers has a world championship held every year in England.» What does conkers mean in this sentence? | A type of cake | *A children's game with a string | A tree in a park | A spiky green case
exercise: Ellie says conkers are good to eat, like sweet chestnuts. What should you tell her? | *Conkers are poisonous, so do not eat them | Yes, eat as many as you like | Only eat them when they are cooked | Conkers are a kind of sweet
test: Which phrase means to take part in the game? | Collect conkers | Eat conkers | A conker case | *Play conkers
test: Which statement is true? | Conkers keep spiders away | Conkers are poisonous to eat | Conkers grow on sweet chestnut trees | *Conkers are the seeds of the horse chestnut
exam: «She came down in the end, with conkers in every pocket and a rip in her trousers.» What does conkers mean here? | A spiky green case | A sweet | *Shiny brown seeds from a horse chestnut tree | A children's game
